From: The FBC Agent <thefbcspecialagent@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 20:02:34 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] input: mouse+keyboard pad through SDL window events (relative
 mouse mode)

mkb_input.c builds on every host. With the SDL window (POSIX, and Windows
with XBOX_SDL_WINDOW) the window thread hands each event to mkb_sdl_event()
after the title's event hook and before the key table, and mkb_sdl_tick()
turns SDL's relative mouse mode on only while the window has the keyboard
focus, F9 has not released it and no overlay owns the input
(mkb_set_overlay). The Win32 raw-input thread stays for the GDI build.
Held mouse buttons now stay held between polls (raw input only reports
transitions), and either Shift/Ctrl counts for the stick clicks.
RECOMP_MKB_TRACE=1 logs relative-mode changes and drained deltas.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ahYm8JBvCH5KhgtSu9Yoy
